      "message": "It took me some time to understand why this was necessary because naively, I thought that you could simply sub-slice the `CStr` and pass it to `fdt.node()` but that\u0027s not possible because it requires a terminating `\u0027\\0\u0027`! So the options you have are\n\n1. modify the original `CStr` to inject the `\u0027\\0\u0027` -\u003e bad w.r.t. mutability\n1. copy the subslice into its own `CStr` -\u003e wasteful\n\nWould you mind describing this problem you\u0027re solving, in the commit message?",
